@gfornax have you looked at nightscout-reporter (https://github.com/zreptil/nightscout-reporter)
it is based on nightscout server (which can be deployed within own perimeters onPrem or in a trusted cloud) and a HTML/JS + PHP based nightscout-reporter.
I'm also faced with such requests and i try to answer them this way......

@mikelperezalbeniz yes there is.
After applying the patch for xdrip+ (which sends the multi-insulin data as an extension to the treatment data structure to nightscout server) a started writing a multi insulin patch for nightscout-reporter (https://github.com/gruoner/nightscout-reporter/tree/Feature-MultipleInsulin) but it isn't finished yet. Some further features need to be implemented to finish the "multiple insulin train".
But u can check it out and use it on your own premise.....

i was afraid of some kind of error like yours....
Deploying nightscout reporter is a bit difficult (see https://github.com/zreptil/nightscout-reporter/issues/42).
I'm not familiar with heroku - i use my own infrastructure with LXD containers. But when u have got a virtual machine with a "normal" webserver (nginx, apache) and PHP support and u have ssh access to that machine:
- u can use my "base.mine" branch
- merge it with the "Feature-*" branches u prefer
- to our own repo (name it as you want; but please don't use "master")
- clone your repo branch locally (where u can compile dart code) and
- change the deploy.sh (i hope your machine is linux) to match our machine name, proxy (if u have one) and account name etc.
- and run the deploy script (beforehand u should "read" the script to see and understand what it is doing)

This deploy.sh script does everything needed to deploy nightscout reporter to my env (i have 3 stages DEV, REF and PROD).
I use nginx and php-fpm natively installed by ubuntu 18.04 with a very simple nginx config
_location /NightScoutReporter {
                root /home/myroot/Software;
                location ~ \.php$ {
                        include snippets/fastcgi-php.conf;
                        fastcgi_pass unix:/run/php/php7.2-fpm.sock;
                }
        }_

IMPORTANT:
when merging my branches together, start with the feature branches and merge "base.mine" at last....
